moon knight is the upcoming disney plus  series that stars oscar isaac as mark  spector aka moon knight one of the more  unique characters in marvel comics this  former mercenary suffers from a  dissociative identity disorder that has  manifested in different ways over the  years in one iteration of the character  spectre saw visions of spider-man  wolverine and captain america guiding  him as he fought crime based on the  official trailer it looks like the show  will put its own spin on the character  for starters the series begins with mark  living under another of his identities a  bumbling museum gift shop employee named  steven grant who seemingly has no memory  of his other selves one day stephen  begins experiencing dream-like visions  that convince him he's losing his mind  but then he realizes the visions are  actually real i can't tell the  difference  between my waking life  and dreams in some of them steven  appears as a grey cloak to moon knight a  vigilante for the egyptian moon guard  konchu any superhero is only as good as  their villain and the official moon  knight trailer finally revealed who the  moon knight will be facing dr arthur  harrow even die hard marvel heads might  not be familiar with the not so good  doctor so here's a quick explainer  dr harrow appears in just one issue of  the moon knight comics the second issue  of volume 2 which was published in 1985.  in the comics he's a nobel prize  nominated researcher who specializes in  pain tolerance upon his nomination for  the nobel prize in medicine he begins to  draw the suspicions of one doctor  victoria graham she doesn't believe he's  been able to accomplish all that he's  done on animal test subjects alone she  makes a shocking realization he's been  using human test subjects against their  will with experiments inspired by nazi  researchers who wanted to make humans  invulnerable to pain  all of this is spearheaded by the  sinister think tank known as omnium  fortunately dr grayl has back up in a  big way mark specter receives a vision  informing him of dr harrow's true  intentions  the two team up to break into dr  harrow's laboratory to stop his evil  ways once and for all although dr harrow  escapes in the story he hasn't popped up  in the comics since but he's about to  make a grand debut once again in the  disney plus series moon knight while  it's easy to catch up with the law  surrounding dr harrow it's unclear how  much good it will do in the lead up to  the latest marvel show based on the  trailer alone it would seem there are  some distinct differences between the dr  harrow from the comics and the one being  played by ethan hawke to begin the comic  version of dr harrow suffers from a  condition called trigeminal neuralgia  which results in facial paralysis it  also causes the left side of his mouth  to remain in a permanent grimace it  would seem like the disney plus  iteration doesn't have the disease but  anything could happen over the course of  6 episodes additionally the moonlight  trailer suggests dr harrow will be a  cult leader as well as a researcher if  the legions of fans bowing to his whim  are any indication ethan hawke himself  actually confirmed that cult leader  status in an interview with seth meyers  the actor stated i've based my character  on david correct have you really  yeah koresh was the leader of the branch  davidians claiming to be a final prophet  he played an integral role in the waco  siege of 1993  ultimately resulting in his death in  terms of what calls dr harrow could lead  in the disney plus series it's possible  it's the cult of kancho in the comics  this is the egyptian deity who gives  moon knight his powers and in the modern  day versions of the character he has a  cult of his own after all dr harrow  encourages mark spector to embrace the  chaos so perhaps he wants to use the  next avatar of konshu for his own  nefarious ends more will undoubtedly be  revealed about the character in the  following weeks otherwise disney plus  and marvel studios have kept their plans  for the character and the raps we'll  know more when moon knight premieres on  march 30th 2022  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the marvel cinematic universe are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one
 

